					<![CDATA[
						 <p>This epitomizes the problem with a lot of meta articles for me. The meta aspect is there for no particular reason. I mean, it doesn't relate to the article itself in anyway, which is a vague piece about consciousness without any kind of context to make it remotely interesting. The footnote commentary is unpleasantly immature (I'm assuming it was meant to be funny?). Also, the coding thing was initially cute, but now with all these offsets, it's messy and a pain to read.</p> <p>Also, what's the joke here?</p> 
